@startuml sequence-oai-record-sync
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: the datestamp of an OAI record moves only when the projected record
'       changes: OaiRecordSync re-projects the entry, compares a fingerprint
'       and writes the new datestamp in its own short transaction, so a reader
'       opening a book (which saves the entry) never re-sends the record, and
'       a deleted or withdrawn entry leaves a tombstone.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, proposal (IP-033). Scope: a metadata edit, a
'       read, a delete, the nightly reconcile. Omitted: retries, tracing.
' Source: apps/core/touch.py, apps/files/views.py (popularity by UPDATE in both
'         download views since issue 214, 2026-11-18),
'         apps/core/models/acquisition.py:138 (touch_entry),
'         apps/files/tests/test_versioned_covers.py (a read no longer saves the entry),
'         OAI-PMH 2.0 spec §2.5.1, §2.7.1 (2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Keeping oai_records in step: fingerprint decides the datestamp (proposal IP-033, 2026-11-16)

actor "Librarian ·\nreader" as actor
database "core tables" as core
participant "Signal receivers" as receivers
queue "Celery" as celery
participant "OaiRecordSync" as sync
participant "Projector" as projector
database "oai_records" as records
participant "Beat" as beat

== metadata edit (title, authors, categories, files, renames) ==
actor -> core : save Entry · EntryAuthor · Author ·\nCategory · Acquisition · categories.add()
core -> receivers : post_save · m2m_changed
receivers -> celery : on_commit: oai.sync(affected entry ids)
celery -> sync : sync([entry_id])
sync -> projector : project(entry) + setSpecs
projector --> sync : RecordProjection
sync -> sync : fingerprint = sha256(canonical JSON\n+ crosswalk version)
sync -[$accent_msg()]> records : <b>UPDATE … SET projection, setSpecs, fingerprint,</b>\n<b>datestamp = date_trunc('second', now())</b>\n<b>WHERE entry_id = … AND fingerprint <> new (autocommit)</b>

== a reader opens the book ==
actor -> core : UPDATE entries SET popularity = popularity + 1\n(QuerySet.update, no save, no post_save; issue 214)
note right of core : no signal, no OAI sync:\nthe projection does not carry popularity

== entry deleted, or its catalog withdrawn ==
actor -> core : delete Entry (or Catalog cascade,\nor catalog opted out)
core -> receivers : post_delete (per entry) · post_save Catalog
receivers -> celery : on_commit: oai.sync(entry_ids)
celery -> sync : sync(entry_ids)
sync -> records : deleted = true, projection = null,\ndatestamp = now (tombstone kept)

== nightly reconcile ==
beat -> sync : reconcile()
sync -> core : every exposed entry id (batches of 200)
sync -> sync : sync(batch): catches QuerySet.update(),\nbulk changes, crosswalk upgrades
sync -> records : rows whose entry no longer exists\nor is not exposed → tombstone

caption Entry.updated_at and touched_at move on every save, including saves that change nothing a harvester sees, so they cannot be OAI datestamps. The fingerprint of the stored\nprojection can: it changes exactly when a harvester would see a different record (§2.7.1), set membership included. The datestamp is\nwritten by a single autocommit statement after the edit committed, so a harvester's cursor does not skip it.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersCatalog · docs/diagrams/sequence-oai-record-sync.puml
@enduml
